For Next.js (App Router), create a single catch-all route at `app/api/chat/[[...path]]/route.ts` with `chatcopsNext()` (see [Fetch runtimes](/server/fetch-runtimes/#nextjs-app-router)):

```typescript
import { chatcopsNext } from '@chatcops/server/next';

export const runtime = 'edge';

export const { POST, OPTIONS } = chatcopsNext({
  provider: {
    type: 'openai',
    apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!,
  },
  systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful assistant.',
  allowedOrigins: ['*'],
  sessionSecrets: [process.env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET!],
});
```

The single catch-all route answers both the chat requests at `/api/chat` and session requests at `/api/chat/session`, so no second route file is needed.

