<source id="1" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/storage/" title="Storage" section="Vector stores &gt; Upstash Vector">
Storage > Vector stores > Upstash Vector

The Upstash store uses an existing dense index configured for cosine distance. Set its dimensions to match your embedder. The store preserves the page source in reserved metadata fields, so `deleteBySource()` can remove all of a page's chunks. Configure a dedicated test index with at least four dimensions to run conformance; tests do not reset the index.

```bash
npm install @chatcops/store-upstash-vector @upstash/vector
```

```typescript
import { memoryStorage } from '@chatcops/core';
import { Index } from '@upstash/vector';
import { upstashVectors } from '@chatcops/store-upstash-vector';

const dimensions = 1024;
const index = new Index({
  url: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_URL!,
  token: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_TOKEN!,
});
const storage = {
  ...memoryStorage(),
  vectors: upstashVectors({ index, dimensions }),
};
```

Metadata filters require every key to match and accept any value in an array. For sparse indexes and hybrid indexes with a sparse text embedding model, pass `keywordSearch: true` to expose `keywordQuery`. Dense indexes leave that method absent. The SDK does not encode the configured index kind in its `Index` type, so only enable this option for supported indexes.
</source>
<source id="2" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/storage/" title="Storage" section="Redis &gt; Upstash">
Storage > Redis > Upstash

```bash
npm install @chatcops/server @chatcops/store-redis @upstash/redis
```

```typescript
import { Redis } from '@upstash/redis';
import { chatcopsMiddleware } from '@chatcops/server';
import { redisStorage } from '@chatcops/store-redis';

const redis = Redis.fromEnv();
const storage = redisStorage({
  redis,
  prefix: 'chatcops',
  conversationTtlMs: 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000,
});

const handler = chatcopsMiddleware({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
  },
  systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful customer support assistant.',
  sessionSecrets: [process.env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET!],
  storage,
});
```
</source>
<source id="3" url="https://chat.codercops.com/getting-started/index-your-site/" title="Index Your Site" section="3. Connect the index to your bot">
Index Your Site > 3. Connect the index to your bot

For Vercel, use the same Upstash index and Redis database as the CLI config:

```typescript
import { chatcopsVercelHandler } from '@chatcops/server';
import { hybridRetriever, openaiEmbedder, retrieverKnowledge } from '@chatcops/core';
import { Redis } from '@upstash/redis';
import { Index } from '@upstash/vector';
import { redisStorage } from '@chatcops/store-redis';
import { upstashVectors } from '@chatcops/store-upstash-vector';

const embedder = openaiEmbedder({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY! });
const redis = new Redis({
  url: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL!,
  token: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN!,
});
const index = new Index({
  url: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_URL!,
  token: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_TOKEN!,
});
const vectors = upstashVectors({ index, dimensions: embedder.dimensions, keywordSearch: true });

export default chatcopsVercelHandler({
  provider: { type: 'claude', apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY! },
  systemPrompt: 'Answer questions about our website using the indexed pages.',
  sessionSecrets: [process.env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET!],
  storage: { ...redisStorage({ redis }), vectors },
  knowledge: [retrieverKnowledge(hybridRetriever({ store: vectors, embedder }))],
});
```

For a Cloudflare Worker, pass its D1 and Vectorize bindings to the storage adapter. Keep the handler between requests so the same store and embedder are reused:
</source>
<source id="4" url="https://chat.codercops.com/getting-started/index-your-site/" title="Index Your Site" section="1. Choose where to keep the index &gt; Vercel with Upstash Vector">
Index Your Site > 1. Choose where to keep the index > Vercel with Upstash Vector

Start with [`@chatcops/store-upstash-vector` setup](https://github.com/codercops/chatcops/tree/dev/packages/store-upstash-vector#readme). Create an Upstash **hybrid** index with cosine distance and the same dimension as the embedder. Hybrid search also needs a persistent key-value store for the ingest manifest; this example uses Upstash Redis.

```bash
npm install @chatcops/core @chatcops/cli @chatcops/store-upstash-vector @chatcops/store-redis @upstash/vector @upstash/redis
```

Create `chatcops.config.ts`. Set `UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_URL`, `UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_TOKEN`, `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL`, `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`, and `OPENAI_API_KEY` in your environment:

```typescript
import { openaiEmbedder } from '@chatcops/core';
import { defineConfig } from '@chatcops/cli';
import { Redis } from '@upstash/redis';
import { Index } from '@upstash/vector';
import { redisStorage } from '@chatcops/store-redis';
import { upstashVectors } from '@chatcops/store-upstash-vector';

const embedder = openaiEmbedder({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY! });
const redis = new Redis({
  url: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL!,
  token: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN!,
});
const index = new Index({
  url: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_URL!,
  token: process.env.UPSTASH_VECTOR_REST_TOKEN!,
});
const vectors = upstashVectors({ index, dimensions: embedder.dimensions, keywordSearch: true });

export default defineConfig({
  embedder,
  storage: { ...redisStorage({ redis }), vectors },
  ingest: {
    sources: [{ type: 'directory', path: './content', baseUrl: 'https://your-site.example' }],
  },
});
```
</source>
<source id="5" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/storage/" title="Storage" section="Redis">
Storage > Redis

The Redis store is provided by `@chatcops/store-redis`. It is currently private and will ship with the next release. The package supports both Upstash and `ioredis` clients and implements conversations, counters, KV locks, and events.
</source>
